<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="8.01" level="1">Civil Remedies and Procedure</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="3" level="2">Actions</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="2" level="3">Actions on Contracts Generally</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>8.01-33</section_number>
	<catch_line>Equitable relief in certain cases</catch_line>
	<text>
		A court shall not grant equitable relief in a suit upon a bond, note, or writing, by an assignee or holder thereof, unless it appears that the plaintiff had no adequate remedy thereon at law.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 8-518; 1977, c. 617; 2005, c. 681.</history>
</law>
